data primitive_identity_d0_scope_note: String = "D0 is NOT terminal acceptance and does NOT close the subject universe. Landed and executing: join mechanism across five carriers, five refusal variants typed, three refusal detectors executing with witnesses (see primitive_d0_refusal_execution_note), derived census across all five surfaces including InterpreterDispatch from gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface. D1 (interpreter-primitive-roster consumption): measurement scaffold deleted; primitive_surface_census_derived reads the roster authority. Population-wide identity join closure remains the terminal acceptance bar."

data primitive_d0_refusal_execution_note: String = "Five PrimitiveJoinViolation variants typed at D0. Three detectors execute with RED witnesses: primitive_surface_missing_identity_violation, primitive_realization_unknown_primitive_violation, primitive_duplicate_semantic_definition_violation. Two scaffold detectors execute on planted inputs only (terminal join expands population-wide detection): primitive_surface_joins_two_identities_violation, primitive_incompatible_invocation_assignment_violation."

data primitive_identity_d2_note: String = "D2 (primitive projection authority): the join gains the question a callable-resolution wall actually asks -- given a DECLARATION, is it the modeled surface of a PRIMITIVE, and are the two ONE authority or genuinely two. primitive_projection_for_declaration is total over every DeclarationRef; ProjectionFidelity separates a host-realized seam from a modeled projection from a divergent one, and only the first two mean one authority. Consumer: the bare-call candidate collector in gunbc#8952, whose first corpus run refused 1215 sites across five names precisely because a modeled std surface and the primitive it projects were two co-candidates with no relation between them. D2 also replaces the prose open denominator with a counted one: primitive_undisposed_surface_symbol_count enumerates, at symbol grain, how far the five-surface census is from the terminal bar. It does NOT close that bar -- see primitive_undisposed_residue_note."

data primitive_identity_d0_note: String = "D0 (primitive-identity-join first slice): semantic primitive identity is ONE join key across five independently-writable surfaces. See primitive_identity_d0_scope_note — NOT the closing contract. primitive_surface_census_derived reads five live authorities including InterpreterDispatch from gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface. Open denominator receipt: primitive_d0_open_denominator_receipt. Dissolve-on: feature:primitive-realization-single-authority."

data primitive_d0_derived_surface_drift_audit_note: String = "Derived-surface drift audit (review 45947 class): AlgebraTemplate — CLOSED, all_algebra_field_templates flat_maps all_algebra_profiles (2c9c01351). EmitHandler — single authority, rt_function_registry with derived rt_functions/rt_ref_map_functions projections (no parallel roster). BuiltinRegistry — OPEN parallel enumeration: builtin_registry_surface_names hand list beside builtin_function_registry Map (witness cannot map_keys Node at runtime; builtin_registry_surface_names_note). PrimitiveContractRow — OPEN parallel enumeration: primitive_contract_roster hand list beside *_contract data rows (primitive_contract_roster_note). D0 mutation control on those two surfaces discovers drift only when the hand list is updated, not when the primary authority grows alone."

data primitive_d0_open_denominator_receipt_note: String = "Typed located counted denominator (rung-honesty receipt): derived_surface_authority_count=5 (BuiltinRegistry, PrimitiveContractRow, AlgebraTemplate, EmitHandler, InterpreterDispatch); open_surface_authority_count=0; interpreter dispatch rows/arm-identities/spellings derived from gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface counters (v1_interpreter_row_count, distinct_arm_identity_count, authored_spelling_count). primitive_d0_interpreter_census_matches_roster links census to roster authority. derived_census_rows_missing_identity_count is measured live by primitive_d0_derived_rows_missing_identity_count — ranks join work remaining on derived surfaces. See primitive_d0_derived_surface_drift_audit_note for per-surface drift status."

data primitive_d0_derived_surface_authority_count: Int = 5

data primitive_d0_open_surface_authority_count: Int = 0

data primitive_d0_parallel_roster_surface_authority_count: Int = 2

data primitive_d0_mutation_control_coverage_note: String = "D1 mutation-control coverage: DISCOVERED on AlgebraTemplate, EmitHandler, and InterpreterDispatch — new template, emit-handler, or interpreter-dispatch row without identity join appears on primitive_surface_census_derived and can refuse. PARTIAL on BuiltinRegistry and PrimitiveContractRow (parallel_roster_surface_authority_count=2) — mutation control fires when the hand roster (builtin_registry_surface_names, primitive_contract_roster) is updated, NOT when builtin_function_registry or a *_contract data row grows alone; see primitive_d0_derived_surface_drift_audit_note. Counted: open_surface_authority_count=0. Derived does not mean complete; parallel roster does not mean single-authority."

data primitive_interpreter_dispatch_roster_note: String = "Interpreter dispatch is seven dispatch symbols in v1_interpreter (gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface): eval_builtin_inner; eval_algebra_method_inner; eval_call (bridge families plus native fold intercept); try_v2_std_collection_map_primitive_grounding; try_parse_table_memo_dispatch; eval_method_call lookup short-circuit; eval_service_call Filesystem.Read carve-out. Row/arm-identity/spelling denominators are v1_interpreter_row_count, distinct_arm_identity_count, authored_spelling_count on the roster authority — not duplicated here. primitive_interpreter_surface_rows derives from v1_interpreter_primitive_arms with provenance DerivedFromAuthority."

data primitive_interpreter_surface_unenumerable_finding_note: String = "Finding (inherits to v1 exit lane): the interpreter primitive surface was six hand-written Rust dispatch sites in v1_interpreter, not one. v1_interpreter eval_builtin_inner is the main free-call site. v2.compiler.eval v2_eval_call_primitive (carrier src/v2/compiler/05_eval.dag) is a separate v2 witness hook — real symbol, NOT v1 dispatch (§3 cite-the-symbol: never attribute it to v1_interpreter.rs). eval_call native intercept for fold_list fires before eval_builtin_inner — explains registry absence. clever-crab-111 macro authority may make eval_builtin_inner derivable sooner; five other sites remain hand-declared until macro dissolves them."

data primitive_fold_list_spelling_fork_note: String = "Named finding — SPELLING FORK, not alias: contract/algebra carry fold while interpreter/emit carry fold_list. Distinct from alias groups (length/count/size are one eval_builtin_inner arm with three spellings — aliases sharing an arm cannot disagree). fold and fold_list are separate surfaces that CAN disagree; fold_list additionally lives on eval_call intercept before eval_builtin_inner, so it never reaches builtin_function_registry."

// Named finding — first two-realizations-one-name specimen: lookup has eval_method_call short-circuit AND an algebra template arm; the short-circuit shadows the algebra arm. Better join specimen than index_by for SurfaceJoinsTwoIdentities / realization reconciliation. keys and values DO have algebra template arms — determinism undetectability is about the lens view of unqualified symbols, not absence of algebra arms.
// WHY THE SIGNATURE IS A GROUNDING AND NOT A COPY. The semantic half of a primitive --
// what it takes and what it returns -- already exists for part of the population, on
// std.algebra AlgebraFieldTemplate.param_types. Landing a second param_types here would
// answer "what does map take" from two sets of bytes, which is the section 3 fork this
// carrier exists to remove. So the contract carries a KEY into the one authority, never
// its contents, and every parameter fact is read back through primitive_signature.
type PrimitiveSignatureGrounding
  = GroundedInAlgebraTemplate { profile: AlgebraProfile }
  | SignatureUngrounded { reason: NonEmptyStr }

// WHY THE KEY CARRIES A PROFILE. Measured over the 90 AlgebraFieldTemplate rows: 23 of the
// 59 distinct names carry more than one row, and several disagree in what they take --
// get is [ReceiverSelf, NamedTemplate{Int}] on the List profile and [ReceiverSelf, ReceiverKey]
// on the two Map-shaped profiles; join carries three signatures; member disagrees in ARITY OUTRIGHT
// (2 on FinitePowerSet, 1 on PointwisePower). Those are receiver-polymorphic operations, not
// duplicates: both readings of get are correct. A projection keyed on canonical_name alone
// would therefore have to pick one silently, which is the same last-import-wins shape the
// namespace lane already carries as a structural hole. The profile is what makes the
// projection a function.
type PrimitiveSemanticContract {
  canonical_name: NonEmptyStr
  signature: PrimitiveSignatureGrounding
}

// The four states of asking a contract for its signature, kept apart on purpose. Absent and
// Ambiguous are different failures with opposite repairs -- Absent means the named template
// does not exist on that profile (a wrong key), Ambiguous means the profile did not
// disambiguate (a key that is not specific enough) -- and NotGrounded is neither: it is a
// contract that never claimed an algebra signature at all. Collapsing any pair of these into
// one reason symbol is the not-applicable-versus-malformed conflation.
type PrimitiveSignatureResolution
  = SignatureResolved {
      parameters: List<AlgebraTypeTemplate>
      result: AlgebraTypeTemplate
    }
  | SignatureAmbiguousOnProfile {
      canonical_name: NonEmptyStr
      candidate_count: Int
    }
  | SignatureAbsentFromProfile { canonical_name: NonEmptyStr }
  | SignatureNotGrounded { reason: NonEmptyStr }

// The resolver takes its candidate rows as a PARAMETER rather than reaching for
// algebra_templates_for_profile itself, and that is a correctness requirement, not a style
// choice. SignatureAmbiguousOnProfile is unoccupied today -- measured, zero duplicate names
// within any of the eight profiles -- but the mechanism that would occupy it is live, because
// the template lists are hand-authored and nothing forbids a repeated row. An arm whose RED
// cannot be produced is a decoration (DESIGN section 4b); threading the candidates through a
// parameter is what keeps that RED authorable by a fixture, which is the boundary section 4b
// says decides the question. Zero occupancy is a quiet guard, not a dead one.
fn algebra_signature_from_candidates(
  canonical_name: NonEmptyStr,
  candidates: List<AlgebraFieldTemplate>
) -> PrimitiveSignatureResolution {
  let matches = candidates |> filter(t => t.name == canonical_name)
  let n = matches |> count
  if n == 0 {
    SignatureAbsentFromProfile { canonical_name: canonical_name }
  } else if n > 1 {
    SignatureAmbiguousOnProfile { canonical_name: canonical_name, candidate_count: n }
  } else {
    match matches |> first {
      Present { value: t } =>
        SignatureResolved { parameters: t.param_types, result: t.return_type }
      Absent =>
        SignatureAbsentFromProfile { canonical_name: canonical_name }
    }
  }
}

// Total over every contract: a contract that never claimed an algebra signature answers
// NotGrounded, which is a different state from a claim that failed to resolve.
fn primitive_signature(contract: PrimitiveSemanticContract) -> PrimitiveSignatureResolution {
  match contract.signature {
    SignatureUngrounded { reason: r } => SignatureNotGrounded { reason: r }
    GroundedInAlgebraTemplate { profile: p } =>
      algebra_signature_from_candidates(
        canonical_name: contract.canonical_name,
        candidates: algebra_templates_for_profile(profile: p)
      )
  }
}

// ARITY IS DERIVED AND HAS NO FIELD. There is deliberately no arity: Int anywhere in this
// module. A stored arity is a hand transcription that rots the first time the signature it
// describes changes -- the decorative-roster failure gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface
// arm_accepted_shape_gap_note refuses an Int for -- so arity exists only as the length of the
// parameter list it is the length of. An unresolved signature therefore has NO arity rather
// than a guessed one: the absent arm returns Absent, not zero, because a primitive taking no
// arguments and a primitive whose signature did not resolve are different facts.
fn primitive_arity(contract: PrimitiveSemanticContract) -> Int? {
  match primitive_signature(contract: contract) {
    SignatureResolved { parameters: ps, result: _ } => Present { value: ps |> count }
    SignatureAmbiguousOnProfile { canonical_name: _, candidate_count: _ } => none
    SignatureAbsentFromProfile { canonical_name: _ } => none
    SignatureNotGrounded { reason: _ } => none
  }
}

fn primitive_signature_is_resolved(contract: PrimitiveSemanticContract) -> Bool {
  match primitive_signature(contract: contract) {
    SignatureResolved { parameters: _, result: _ } => true
    SignatureAmbiguousOnProfile { canonical_name: _, candidate_count: _ } => false
    SignatureAbsentFromProfile { canonical_name: _ } => false
    SignatureNotGrounded { reason: _ } => false
  }
}

// THE POPULATION IS DERIVED, NOT ENUMERATED. Zero rows are authored here: the semantic
// contracts ARE the algebra template rows, read at their own grain. That is what keeps this
// surface off the parallel-hand-roster failure the sibling surfaces carry (see
// primitive_d0_derived_surface_drift_audit_note) -- there is no second list to drift from,
// because there is no second list. 87 rows over 59 distinct names; the gap is the 21
// receiver-polymorphic names, and it is the reason the key is a pair.
fn algebra_grounded_semantic_contracts() -> List<PrimitiveSemanticContract> {
  all_algebra_profiles()
    |> flat_map(profile =>
        algebra_templates_for_profile(profile: profile)
          |> map(t => PrimitiveSemanticContract {
               canonical_name: t.name as NonEmptyStr,
               signature: GroundedInAlgebraTemplate { profile: profile }
             })
      )
}

fn algebra_grounded_semantic_contract_count() -> Int {
  algebra_grounded_semantic_contracts() |> count
}

// TOTALITY: every derived contract resolves to exactly one signature. This is the (a) claim,
// and its RED is authorable as data at the fixture boundary -- a grounding naming a
// (canonical_name, profile) pair carrying no template resolves Absent and reds this.
fn algebra_grounded_signatures_all_resolve() -> Bool {
  algebra_grounded_semantic_contracts() |> all(c => primitive_signature_is_resolved(contract: c))
}

// THE GROUNDINGS THAT CAN ACTUALLY BE WRONG. The fold above walks contracts DERIVED from the
// template rows, so it can only fail if the derivation itself breaks -- it is nearly
// tautological. The declared definitions are the opposite: their profile is authored BY HAND,
// so a template that moves between profiles upstream leaves the hand-written key pointing at
// nothing, and the resolution silently becomes Absent. That is not hypothetical -- it happened:
// map_keys and map_values were relocated from PartialFunction to FinitelySupportedFunction
// upstream, and nothing in this module noticed until a merge forced a recompile. This fold is
// the guard that would have caught it, and it covers exactly the rows a human typed.
fn declared_definition_groundings_all_dispose() -> Bool {
  primitive_declared_definitions()
    |> all(d =>
        match primitive_signature(contract: d.semantic_contract) {
          SignatureResolved { parameters: _, result: _ } => true
          SignatureNotGrounded { reason: _ } => true
          SignatureAmbiguousOnProfile { canonical_name: _, candidate_count: _ } => false
          SignatureAbsentFromProfile { canonical_name: _ } => false
        }
      )
}

type PrimitiveDefinition {
  identity: PrimitiveIdentity
  semantic_contract: PrimitiveSemanticContract
}

type InvocationForm
  = FreeCall
  | MethodCall { receiver_domain: NonEmptyStr }
  | OperatorCall

type PrimitiveInvocationSurface {
  primitive: PrimitiveIdentity
  form: InvocationForm
  authored_symbol: NonEmptyStr
}

type RealizationTarget
  = InterpreterHost
  | EmitRust
  | EmitTypeScript

type PrimitiveRealization {
  primitive: PrimitiveIdentity
  target: RealizationTarget
  handler: DeclarationRef
}

type PrimitiveCostFact {
  primitive: PrimitiveIdentity
  cost: CostShape
}

type TraversalOrder
  = HostUnspecifiedOrder
  | CanonicalOrder
  | SourcePreservingOrder
  | OrderFreeResult
  | TraversalOrderUnclassified

type PrimitiveTraversalOrderFact {
  primitive: PrimitiveIdentity
  order: TraversalOrder
}

type PrimitiveSurfaceAuthority
  = BuiltinRegistry
  | PrimitiveContractRow
  | AlgebraTemplate
  | InterpreterDispatch
  | EmitHandler

type PrimitiveSurfaceCensusProvenance
  = DerivedFromAuthority
  | MeasurementOnly

type PrimitiveSurfaceRow {
  authority: PrimitiveSurfaceAuthority
  authored_symbol: NonEmptyStr
  authority_ref: DeclarationRef
  primitive: PrimitiveIdentity?
  provenance: PrimitiveSurfaceCensusProvenance
}

type PrimitiveJoinViolation
  = SurfaceMissingPrimitiveIdentity {
      authority: PrimitiveSurfaceAuthority
      authored_symbol: NonEmptyStr
    }
  | SurfaceJoinsTwoIdentities {
      authority: PrimitiveSurfaceAuthority
      authored_symbol: NonEmptyStr
      first: PrimitiveIdentity
      second: PrimitiveIdentity
    }
  | IncompatibleInvocationAssignment {
      authored_symbol: NonEmptyStr
      first: PrimitiveIdentity
      second: PrimitiveIdentity
    }
  | RealizationNamesUnknownPrimitive {
      target: RealizationTarget
      handler: DeclarationRef
    }
  | DuplicateSemanticDefinition { identity: PrimitiveIdentity }

fn primitive_identity_eq(left: PrimitiveIdentity, right: PrimitiveIdentity) -> Bool {
  left.slug == right.slug
}

data primitive_map_keys: PrimitiveIdentity = primitive_identity_slug(name: "map_keys")
data primitive_sorted_map_keys: PrimitiveIdentity = primitive_identity_slug(name: "sorted_map_keys")
data primitive_map_values: PrimitiveIdentity = primitive_identity_slug(name: "map_values")
data primitive_fold_list: PrimitiveIdentity = primitive_identity_slug(name: "fold_list")
data primitive_index_by: PrimitiveIdentity = primitive_identity_slug(name: "index_by")

data primitive_map_keys_definition: PrimitiveDefinition = PrimitiveDefinition {
  identity: primitive_map_keys,
  semantic_contract: PrimitiveSemanticContract {
    canonical_name: "map_keys" as NonEmptyStr,
    signature: GroundedInAlgebraTemplate { profile: FinitelySupportedFunctionProfile },
  },
}

data primitive_sorted_map_keys_definition: PrimitiveDefinition = PrimitiveDefinition {
  identity: primitive_sorted_map_keys,
  semantic_contract: PrimitiveSemanticContract {
    canonical_name: "sorted_map_keys" as NonEmptyStr,
    signature: SignatureUngrounded {
      reason: "sorted_map_keys is typed by the v1 inference special case beside map_keys, but std.algebra declares no sorted_map_keys template. Grounding it on FinitelySupportedFunctionProfile would resolve SignatureAbsentFromProfile and would falsely claim an algebra surface that does not exist." as NonEmptyStr
    },
  },
}

data primitive_map_values_definition: PrimitiveDefinition = PrimitiveDefinition {
  identity: primitive_map_values,
  semantic_contract: PrimitiveSemanticContract {
    canonical_name: "map_values" as NonEmptyStr,
    signature: GroundedInAlgebraTemplate { profile: FinitelySupportedFunctionProfile },
  },
}

data primitive_fold_list_definition: PrimitiveDefinition = PrimitiveDefinition {
  identity: primitive_fold_list,
  semantic_contract: PrimitiveSemanticContract {
    canonical_name: "fold_list" as NonEmptyStr,
    signature: SignatureUngrounded {
      reason: "spelling fork: algebra carries fold, interpreter and emit carry fold_list, and they are separate surfaces that can disagree -- see primitive_fold_list_spelling_fork_note. Grounding this name on the algebra surface would resolve Absent, and grounding it on the fold row would assert the fork away rather than record it." as NonEmptyStr
    },
  },
}

data primitive_index_by_definition: PrimitiveDefinition = PrimitiveDefinition {
  identity: primitive_index_by,
  semantic_contract: PrimitiveSemanticContract {
    canonical_name: "index_by" as NonEmptyStr,
    signature: SignatureUngrounded {
      reason: "no algebra template arm and no builtin registry row -- index_by is the named registry+algebra dual-absence specimen, so there is no existing signature to project and authoring one here would fabricate it." as NonEmptyStr
    },
  },
}

data primitive_d0_definitions: List<PrimitiveDefinition> = [
  primitive_map_keys_definition,
  primitive_sorted_map_keys_definition,
  primitive_map_values_definition,
  primitive_fold_list_definition,
  primitive_index_by_definition,
]

fn surface_row(
  authority: PrimitiveSurfaceAuthority,
  authored_symbol: String,
  authority_ref: DeclarationRef,
  primitive: PrimitiveIdentity?,
  provenance: PrimitiveSurfaceCensusProvenance
) -> PrimitiveSurfaceRow {
  PrimitiveSurfaceRow {
    authority: authority,
    authored_symbol: authored_symbol as NonEmptyStr,
    authority_ref: authority_ref,
    primitive: primitive,
    provenance: provenance,
  }
}

